==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|ars|lang=goh}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*arsaz}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|de}} {{m|ine-pro|*h₃érsos}}, {{m|ine-pro|*orso-||behind, arse}}. Compare Dutch {{term|aars|lang=nl}}, English {{term|arse|lang=en}}, Norwegian {{term|rass|lang=no}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/⁠ʔaʁʃ/|lang=de}} {{a|standard}}
* {{IPA|/⁠ʔaːʃ/|lang=de}} {{a|widespread, especially northern and central Germany}}
* {{audio|De-Arsch.ogg|Audio|lang=de}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|m|Arsches|gen2=Arschs|Ärsche}}

# {{context|vulgar|lang=de}} [[arse]], [[posterior]], [[buttocks]]

====Usage notes====
* In formal settings, ''Arsch'' is vulgar and inappropriate; in informal settings (e.g. among friends or family) this usually not the case. Note, however, that ''Arsch'' may have a stronger sexual implication than some synonyms, which, in certain contexts, might make the word inappropriate even in informal settings.

